mark german has just given us a massive  amount of new information  on a variety of apple silicon macs  including  the 14 and 16 inch macbook pros  which he says are coming this summer so  yeah if you watch my video where i bet  my goatee  once again on a wwdc reveal of these new  m1x macbook pros  you'll know why i'm so excited about it  but it doesn't stop there because he's  also given us new info  on the new macbook air redesign the  apple silicon mac pro  the mac mini and apparently the new 10  core m1x chip  which is definitely a huge surprise but  i've actually figured out why this new  chip makes  so much sense for apple to do so let's  get right into that first  for many months we believe that the m1x  chip would come with  12 cpu cores based on information from  mark german  who claimed that we would be getting  eight high performance cores  in the next apple silicon chip so we  rightfully assumed that those eight  cores would combine  with the existing four efficiency cores  that we already have  to give us a 12 core m1x chip  which would end up blowing everyone's  mind but  we were wrong the new 10 court ship is  actually gonna be  better than what we thought it would be  and if you think that's  absolutely crazy let me explain the bulk  of the performance  is going to be coming from those eight  performance cores  so losing two efficiency cores isn't  going to be that big of a deal  especially since apple is planning to  use the now freed up space  for something even better apple's m1 soc  package comes with various components  like the processing cores  the graphics cores the neural engine  unified memory  and everything else if apple plans to  add four more performance cores  they're gonna likely need to make the  entire silicon die larger  regardless of whether they get rid of  those two efficiency cores or not  since i'm expecting them to reuse the  same exact m1 cores  from their current max and the issue is  that making the entire die  size larger becomes more expensive and  harder to manufacture  so it seems like apple is ditching two  of those efficiency cores  to make more room for some higher  performance components  specifically mark german says that we'll  be getting up to 64 gigabytes of memory  an improved neural engine and either a  16 or 32 core gpu  so let me break all of that down and  explain what that's going to mean for  you  first off a maximum of 64 gigs of ram  makes sense because that's the current  limit on the 16-inch intel based macbook  pro  so apple seems to want to match it with  the new 16-inch m1x model and as you  guys already know from our videos  apple's unified memory is incredibly  efficient compared to regular old x86  ram  which more easily bottlenecks the  performance of the system  so in my opinion the base 16 gigabyte of  ram  variant on the m1x is going to be more  than enough for almost  everyone out there now as far as the  neural engine an  upgraded model makes sense and it's  going to be a huge deal in the future  especially looking at how much it helped  the m1 macbook air  in an ai based super resolution test  compared to samsung's new galaxy book  pro now going further  mark also mentioned that we're getting  more thunderbolt ports which makes total  sense  so probably either three or four of them  according to leaked schematics  and i'm sure that it's going to support  the same number of displays  as the current intel macbook pros and  now moving on to the graphics  this is what's going to truly blow all  of you away  german says that there will be two  separate chips codenamed  jade c chop and c die one with a 16 core  gpu  and one with 32 cores now i know that  some people online  think that this means that the gpu will  be discrete  and separated from the main chip but  that's wrong  the m1x will be combined into one  single package and here's how apple is  gonna do it  if you take a look at the current m1  chip the unified memory is actually off  to the  side allowing apple to configure it with  either eight gigs or 16 gigs of ram  and there were actually some people who  were able to unsolder the ram  and upgrade it themselves so to solve  the gpu option issue  on the m1x there are actually two  different ways that apple can handle  this  the first way is by doing exactly what  they did with the ram  by attaching the graphics onto the other  side of the chip  in the same manner allowing apple to  configure the  m1x with either a 16 or 32 core gpu  however if apple uses the same exact gpu  cores  from the m1 chip then they wouldn't be  able to fit  32 cores in the same area as  16 cores so the actual package  would undoubtedly have to be larger for  the 32 core variant  because of this i think the second way  makes much more sense  just like mark german said there's gonna  be two separate chips  one with 16 graphics cores that supports  up to 32 gigs of ram  and another physically larger chip with  32 graphics cores  that supports up to 64 gigs of ram  forcing you to upgrade to the larger  chip if you want  all of that ram the only question that's  left unanswered  is whether they'll call both variants  the m1x chip  or maybe mixing it up by calling it the  m1x and  the m1z but i personally think it's  gonna be  the m1x for both but the more important  thing is the performance of those gpus  so let's quickly discuss that when i  estimated the performance of the 16 core  m1x a couple of months ago  we basically confirmed that it would  outperform  the crazy expensive 800 5600  m upgrade on the current 16-inch macbook  pro  which is absolutely insane so if the m1x  actually gets a 32 core gpu option  like mark german says it will we're  looking at graphics performance getting  close to as high  as the vega 2 gpu within the intel based  mac pro  and i have a pretty good feeling that  it's actually going to be faster in  terms of  real-world workflows due to the unified  architecture  but going beyond that some people are  worried that the whole  10 core layout with only two efficiency  cores  is going to be bad for the battery life  but let me explain why i think it's not  going to be an issue  in linus tech tips review of the new m1  macbooks  the air lasted about 13 hours in their  real world  battery life test compared to over 20  hours  for the macbook pro that comes out to  around 53 percent  better battery life which is  mind-blowing because the battery on the  macbook pro  is only around 16 larger than the one  on the macbook air so what this proves  is that the extra 16  in physical battery size was able to  take  the real world battery life a lot  further than expected  so if we consider the fact that the  current 16-inch macbook pro  comes with a 100 watt hour battery  literally twice as large as the one in  the macbook air  i think the battery life on the m1x  16-inch model  is gonna be totally great even with only  two efficiency cores  and according to mark german the 14 and  16 inch pros are both coming  this summer which points to apple  revealing them at their wwdc event  less than three weeks from today so now  with the macbook pros out of the way  let's go ahead and look at the other  products like the new mac mini  which german says will be getting the  same m1x chip options as the macbook  pros  and now it makes total sense why apple  went with only two efficiency cores  since the desktop mac mini doesn't  really need them and that is why  i personally believe that apple will  reveal the new mac mini  alongside the new macbook for a summer  launch  since that's exactly what they did last  november with the m1 max  but i don't know when it's gonna ship  especially since mark said that it could  get delayed but based on everything that  mark said  i fully expect the current m1 mac mini  to stick around  at the same 700 price and then the new  m1x mini  will directly replace the current intel  base model  so you're going to have a choice between  the m1 and the m1x mini and based on all  of that info  and the potential for the m1x chip to  get a 32 core gpu  i fully believe that this same m1x chip  is going to be loaded into the larger  30 inch imac when they reveal that later  this year at another event most likely  in october or  november now as far as the new  redesigned macbook air that we've been  discussing for a while  mark says that it's going to be packed  with a chip that's going to be a direct  successor to the m1 processor which  obviously means  that it's going to be called the m2 chip  with the same number of  cpu cores but they're going to be new  cores  so they're going to be faster the only  surprise that mark gave us  was that the graphics cores will  increase from seven or eight  to nine or ten so basically you're  getting two more graphics cores  based on the model that you're going to  be choosing mark also mentioned that the  lower end base  1300 macbook pro would be getting the  exact same chip  as the new air and i personally believe  that both of them are going to be  revealed  at the same time now mark says that the  air could come as soon as the end of  this year  but i think it could get pushed back  into march of 2022  based on rumors from ming chi quo and  digitimes  now as far as the mac pro mark gave us  some more info on that  now claiming that it's going to look  like a smaller version of the current  mac pro design basically you turning  on his previous claim that it's going to  look like a much taller mac mini  and i think that this makes total sense  because the design of the mac pro  has kind of become iconic and it makes  sense to keep it around  but the mind-blowing thing is that he  says it's going to come with either a 20  or  40 core cpu and either a 64  or 128 core gpu and i personally think  that it's going to be coming sometime  next year most likely in december but  before that happens  we should totally be expecting just one  more intel based  mac pro refresh at the end of this year  in december  using the same exact chassis that we  currently have  but packing new intel xeon iceland chips  and big navi graphics options so there  you guys go  those are my thoughts on mark's latest  report and if you totally disagree with  me  go ahead and comment your thoughts down  below but if you enjoyed the video go  ahead and click the circle above to  subscribe  for more videos like this one definitely  check out one of those two right there  thanks for watching and we'll see you in  the next video
 

